# STATION 11: world control through the game's own systems: <<weather>>, <<time>>, and t() translations.
npc: @test_world
title: Station 11 - Weather, time, translation
speaker: Tester

== start
TEST 11: World. In-game hour: {hour()}. The weather you see: "{weather()}". Translated line: "{t("lowtalk.test.hello")}" (expect: Hello from the language file).
-> Cloudy weather for me only (expect the sky to change within a couple of seconds; other players are unaffected)
    <<weather Zone1_Cloudy_Medium player>>
    <<jump start>>
-> Clear my personal weather (expect the sky to go back to normal)
    <<weather clear player>>
    <<jump start>>
-> Force a storm on the whole world (expect stormy weather for everyone here)
    <<weather Skylands_Rapid_Marsh_Stormy>>
    <<jump start>>
-> Clear the world weather
    <<weather clear>>
    <<jump start>>
-> Jump to midnight (expect instant darkness; the hour above reads 0 on the next menu)
    <<time midnight>>
    <<jump start>>
-> Fade to noon over 5 seconds (expect a smooth sunrise)
    <<time noon 5>>
    <<jump start>>
-> Pause time, then resume (expect the sun to stop; it moves again after Continue)
    <<time pause>>
    Time is paused. Press Continue to resume it.
    <<time resume>>
    <<jump start>>
-> Leave
    <<end>>
